I've been having this crazy recurring  dream lately the dream is about the  future of laptops and computing I know  it's weird but it's of a post PC device  that combines the best of my laptop the  MacBook Air with the best of a tablet  with no compromises but then this weird  thing happened in my dream last week  Microsoft introduced the surface pro 3  and told me the dream had come true with  a larger HD screen a new keyboard and  improved kickstand  and a $7.99 starting price Microsoft is  confident that the surface pro 3 is it  the tablet to replace my tablet but my  beloved 13-inch MacBook Air but while  this surface certainly leaps forward and  bringing the tablet and the laptop  together and bringing the laptop into  the future there are still considerable  compromises you make for getting  everything in one package let's first  talk about the surface as a tablet  Microsoft is calling it a tablet of  course the device is impressively thin  and even with a 12 inch screen it only  weighs 1.76 pounds that's much thinner  than the MacBook Air but not as thin as  Apple's iPad air and not as light either  holding it up to read on can be very  uncomfortable no really my arm feels  like it's gonna fall off right now not  to mention the sides can get really warm  during processor intensive tasks or even  just streaming video that's of course  because inside here are the guts of a  laptop but Microsoft figures you'll be  keeping this on your lap which is why  it's put so much into improving the lap  ability that's a made up Microsoft Word  by the way now you can adjust the  kickstand to your liking to better  position it on your legs  it no longer falls off my lap as much  but because you can't just push back the  screen it takes longer than a laptop to  get just right but the surface doesn't  look or feel like a laptop competitor  till you clicking that keyboard cover  which still oddly is not included with  the surface the type cover cost 130  dollars I really like that the keyboard  can now be propped up instead of laying  completely flat the trackpad has also  been improved and enlarged but it's  still very frustrating to use not only  is it too  small but sometimes scrolling doesn't  work and the cursor can easily jump when  you're typing bottom line you'll want to  use a bluetooth mouse you'll also want  to go shopping for a USB expander or  that $200 docking station since it only  has one USB port and when you start  plugging in those peripherals it starts  looking like it has dreadlocks if you  really want the surface to replace your  laptop the price starts adding up the  mouse the keyboard the docking station  but what Microsoft does include in the  box is a stylus which is useful for  taking notes and pretty fun to play with  but there's no slot for it go in my  dreams  wearing a stylus necklace is very cool  with all that setup the surface becomes  a workhorse everything runs smoothly and  the new aspect ratio of the  high-resolution screen makes it easy to  put windows side-by-side I love that  feature but I still find Windows 8.1  complicated to use and just disjointed  battery life is much better than the  last surface and Microsoft deserves  credit for matching the battery life of  the latest ultra box still it doesn't  live up to the all-day promise the  surface stream video for seven hours  while the MacBook Air lasted nearly nine  and a half hours on the same test but  it's pretty incredible how much power  and features they've crammed into such  an incredibly thin device that said the  pro 3 still suffers from the surface  curse it isn't as good as other tablets  for tablet things and it isn't as good  of a laptop as my MacBook Air so is this  the post PC computer of my dreams no but  it's the closest thing on the market  which means I guess I'll keep having  more crazy dreams
 

